<h2>Who may do what</h2>

<p>Every cell below is one call to <code>$c-&gt;may($action, $doc)</code>,
asked as the page is drawn. A blank cell is a refusal, and the number is the
status <code>$c-&gt;deny</code> would send: <strong>403</strong> when you are
allowed to know the row exists, <strong>404</strong> when you are not.</p>

{% if user %}
<table class="matrix">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>document</th><th>owner</th>
        <th>read</th><th>edit</th><th>publish</th><th>delete</th><th>share</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for doc in docs %}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="/doc/{% doc.id %}">{% doc.title %}</a>
        {% if doc.public %}<span class="tag">public</span>{% end %}</td>
      <td><code>{% doc.owner.email %}</code></td>
      {% for a in doc.actions %}
      <td class="{% if a.may %}yes{% else %}no{% end %}">
        {% if a.may %}yes{% else %}<span class="status">{% a.status %}</span>{% end %}
      </td>
      {% end %}
    </tr>
  {% end %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="quiet">Nobody is signed in, so every rule refuses. Pick somebody
above.</p>
{% end %}

<h2>The documents</h2>

{% for doc in docs %}
<section class="doc">
  <h3>{% doc.title %}</h3>
  <p class="quiet">owned by <code>{% doc.owner.email %}</code>{% if doc.public %},
    and public{% end %}</p>

  {% if doc.shared %}
  <p class="quiet">shared for editing with:
    {% for s in doc.shared %}<code>{% s.email %}</code> {% end %}</p>
  {% end %}

  <div class="actions">
    <form method="post" action="/doc/{% doc.id %}/edit" class="inline">
      <input name="title" value="{% doc.title %}" size="24">
      <button>Edit</button>
    </form>
    <form method="post" action="/doc/{% doc.id %}/publish" class="inline">
      <button>Publish</button>
    </form>
    <form method="post" action="/doc/{% doc.id %}/delete" class="inline">
      <button>Delete</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div class="actions">
    <form method="post" action="/doc/{% doc.id %}/share" class="inline">
      <select name="user_id">
      {% for u in users %}<option value="{% u.id %}">{% u.email %}</option>{% end %}
      </select>
      <button>Grant edit</button>
    </form>
    <form method="post" action="/doc/{% doc.id %}/unshare" class="inline">
      <select name="user_id">
      {% for u in users %}<option value="{% u.id %}">{% u.email %}</option>{% end %}
      </select>
      <button>Revoke</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>
{% end %}

<h2>Things worth trying</h2>

<ol class="try">
  <li>As <code>alice</code>, edit <em>Bob's draft</em>: <strong>404</strong>.
    Not 403 - a 403 on somebody else's id confirms the row is there.</li>
  <li>As <code>alice</code> (a <code>member</code>), publish <em>her own</em>
    notes: <strong>403</strong>. She knows it exists, she is simply not on a
    high enough rung.</li>
  <li>As <code>alice</code>, grant <code>bob</code> edit on her notes, then
    act as <code>bob</code> and edit them. Then revoke, and try again: it
    stops working on the next request, because nothing is cached.</li>
  <li>As <code>carol</code> (an <code>admin</code>), delete anything. Then try
    to grant yourself edit on Alice's notes: <strong>404</strong>. Being an
    admin is not the same as being the owner, which is the difference between
    a role and a grant.</li>
</ol>
